{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And Moses turned and went down from the mountain.</b> Our Rabbi Hananel writes that this teaches that Moses had his face turned toward the cloud, and he descended by the same path he had ascended — just as he ascended with his face toward the cloud that was on the mountain, so too at his descent. And so too was the High Priest on the Day of Atonement when he emerged from the Holy of Holies, as it was taught: ״יצא ובא לו דרך כניסתו״ — he went out and came by the way of his entry; thus they expounded the verse (Leviticus 16:24) ״ואת עולתו ואת עולת העם״ — ״ואת עולתו ואת עולת העם״ — as he entered, so he went out and performed his burnt-offering. And so it is written concerning Solomon (2 Chronicles 1:13) ״ויבא שלמה לבמה אשר בגבעון ירושלם״ — and even though one may say that the word לבמה means מן הבמה, in the manner of what is written (Numbers 31:21) ״הבאים למלחמה״, whose meaning is those who came from the battle — nonetheless such was the actual practice, that at the time of his departure from it he would turn his face toward it just as when he came to it, as it is said (Psalms 16:8) ״שויתי ה׳ לנגדי תמיד״. And from where do we know that the Shekhinah was on the mountain at the time of Moses' descent from the mountain? As it is said (Deuteronomy 9:15) ״ואפן וארד מן ההר וההר בוער באש ושני לוחות הברית על שתי ידי״. And likewise the disciple is obligated, when he takes leave of his master, to walk backward with his face toward his master until he is hidden from him, and so is the custom of all Israel to this day: when they finish their prayer they withdraw backward three paces. End of quote." "<b>ותמצא</b> In this verse together with the verse after it there are 108 words, corresponding to the 108 handbreadths that were in one tablet, and in both of them 216 handbreadths, corresponding to the 216 letters in the 72 names that go out from the Great Name — for the tablets were six long and six wide and three thick; three times 36, that makes 108 handbreadths in each and every tablet. And when the tablets were placed inside the Ark, this is an explicit explanation that the Name was in the Ark with all its combination. And likewise you will find from ויפסול until ויקרא there are 108 letters as well, and afterward Scripture mentions the Name ויעבור ה׳ על פניו — and this is a complete explanation that the Unique Name, from which 72 names emerge, has in them 216 letters — for all this was explicitly explained to Moses at Sinai." "<b>Tablets written on both their sides, from this side and from that side they are written.</b> This was a great wonder: the script could be read in proper order from both sides, unlike our own script, where from the front it is in order but from the back it is reversed. And it says מזה ומזה — from both sides — and they are the front and the back." "<b>And it is possible</b> to interpret משני עבריהם as hinting that the meaning of the words of Torah has two sides, revealed and hidden, in the manner that Solomon, peace be upon him, said (Proverbs 25:11) ״תפוחי זהב במשכיות כסף״, and it is written (Job 11:6) ״כי כפלים לתושיה״ — that the Torah is doubled, and besides the plain senses of the Torah there are in it yet hidden treasures of wisdom. And concerning this the verse says (Psalms 62:12) ״אחת דבר אלהים שתים זו שמעתי״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:26.228361134Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}